# Cursor AI Rules for Portfolio Modernization Project

## 1. Documentation & Context

- **ALWAYS** read `DOCUMENTATION.md` at the start of each session to understand project context, architecture, and current state
- **ALWAYS** reference `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` for current tasks, progress, and next steps
- **ALWAYS** update both documentation files when making architectural changes or completing major tasks
- **ALWAYS** check the current branch and commit status before making changes
- **ALWAYS** reference the original site (tommelloul.com) for visual and behavioral reference

## 2. Visual Parity Requirements

- **MAINTAIN** 100% visual parity with tommelloul.com at all times
- **RUN** visual comparison tests after any major changes using `npm run test:visual`
- **REFERENCE** baseline screenshots in `tests/baseline/` when making layout changes
- **NEVER** introduce visual regressions - if tests fail, fix before proceeding
- **VERIFY** responsive behavior at all breakpoints (375px, 768px, 1920px)
- **MATCH** exact typography, spacing, colors, and animations from original site

## 3. Code Standards & Architecture

- **USE** TypeScript strict mode for all new code
- **FOLLOW** existing component patterns in `src/components/` directory
- **USE** Framer Motion for all animations (no jQuery or vanilla JS animations)
- **USE** Tailwind CSS for styling with custom CSS only when necessary
- **KEEP** components modular, reusable, and properly typed
- **MAINTAIN** consistent file structure and naming conventions
- **USE** forwardRef when components need refs for scroll detection or video control

## 4. Testing Requirements

- **RUN** `npm run test` before committing any changes
- **UPDATE** tests when changing functionality or adding new features
- **ADD** visual comparison tests for any new sections or major layout changes
- **VERIFY** all interactions work identically to original site
- **TEST** responsive behavior at all breakpoints
- **ENSURE** all assets load without 404 errors

## 5. Asset Management

- **STORE** all assets in `/public` directory with proper organization
- **USE** relative paths from `/public` in all code (e.g., `/works/ANIMISM/Render.jpg`)
- **OPTIMIZE** images to WebP/AVIF formats when possible
- **INCLUDE** fallback formats for videos (WebM + MP4)
- **VERIFY** all asset paths are correct and files exist
- **MAINTAIN** consistent naming conventions for assets

## 6. Component Development Patterns

- **USE** forwardRef when components need refs (especially for scroll detection)
- **IMPLEMENT** proper TypeScript interfaces for all props and data structures
- **FOLLOW** existing data structure patterns in `src/lib/data.ts`
- **USE** useInView for scroll-triggered animations and video autoplay
- **MAINTAIN** consistent component structure and naming
- **INCLUDE** proper error handling and loading states

## 7. Video Handling Standards

- **IMPLEMENT** autoplay with useInView detection for background videos
- **ALWAYS** include muted, loop, and playsInline attributes
- **PROVIDE** poster images for all videos
- **INCLUDE** video ref for direct play/pause control
- **HANDLE** autoplay failures gracefully with console.error logging
- **SUPPORT** both WebM and MP4 formats with proper fallbacks

## 8. Plan & Progress Updates

- **MARK** completed tasks in `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` with completion date and commit hash
- **ADD** new tasks as they are identified during development
- **DOCUMENT** all architectural decisions in the Decision Log section
- **UPDATE** Known Issues section when bugs are found or resolved
- **MAINTAIN** accurate progress tracking and time estimates
- **REFERENCE** specific files and line numbers when documenting changes

## 9. Commit Standards

- **USE** conventional commit format: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`
- **REFERENCE** relevant files and components in commit messages
- **UPDATE** plan markdown files before committing
- **KEEP** commits focused and atomic (one logical change per commit)
- **INCLUDE** brief description of what was changed and why
- **VERIFY** all tests pass before committing

## 10. Performance & Optimization

- **LAZY LOAD** images and videos to improve initial page load
- **USE** Next.js Image component when possible for automatic optimization
- **MINIMIZE** bundle size by avoiding unnecessary dependencies
- **OPTIMIZE** animations for 60fps performance
- **IMPLEMENT** proper loading states and error boundaries
- **MONITOR** bundle size with `npm run analyze`

## 11. Original Site Reference

- **REFERENCE** original site files in `/Users/tomba/Documents/tommelloul/` when implementing features
- **STUDY** original CSS in `assets/css/main.css` for exact styling
- **ANALYZE** original JavaScript in `assets/js/` for behavior patterns
- **MATCH** exact layout structure from `index.html`
- **PRESERVE** all original functionality and interactions

## 12. Error Handling & Debugging

- **INCLUDE** proper error handling for all async operations
- **LOG** errors to console with descriptive messages
- **HANDLE** video autoplay failures gracefully
- **PROVIDE** fallbacks for missing assets or failed loads
- **DEBUG** issues systematically using browser dev tools
- **VERIFY** fixes work across all browsers and devices

## 13. Responsive Design

- **TEST** all breakpoints: mobile (375px), tablet (768px), desktop (1920px)
- **MATCH** original responsive behavior exactly
- **USE** Tailwind responsive classes consistently
- **VERIFY** touch interactions work on mobile devices
- **ENSURE** text remains readable at all screen sizes

## 14. Accessibility

- **INCLUDE** proper ARIA labels and roles
- **ENSURE** keyboard navigation works correctly
- **PROVIDE** alt text for all images
- **MAINTAIN** proper focus management
- **SUPPORT** screen readers and assistive technologies
- **FOLLOW** WCAG guidelines for accessibility

## 15. Code Quality

- **WRITE** clean, readable, and maintainable code
- **USE** meaningful variable and function names
- **INCLUDE** comments for complex logic
- **AVOID** code duplication
- **FOLLOW** React best practices and hooks patterns
- **KEEP** functions small and focused on single responsibilities

---

*These rules ensure consistent development practices and maintain the high quality standards required for this portfolio modernization project. Always prioritize visual parity, code quality, and user experience.*
